{"step_index":58,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:29:19Z","input_tokens":4236,"cache_read_tokens":175634,"output_tokens":2252,"content":"I have built the complete **Code Flow Visualizer — Learn Coding Step by Step Without AI APIs** in [`C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer).\n\n> **Workspace Tip:** Open `C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer` as your active workspace, or open [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/index.html) directly in your browser.\n\n---\n\n### What Has Been Built (Sections 1–15)\n\n1. **100% Local, Rule-Based Architecture (Zero AI APIs — Sections 3, 7, 8, 13)**\n   - **Python Execution Engine ([engine.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.py)) & Local Offline Browser Engine ([engine.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.js))**:\n     - Validates syntax and blocks unsupported/unsafe constructs (`import`, `open`, `eval`, `exec`, `async`, `with`, `yield`, `lambda`) before execution ([`validate_python_support`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.py#L49-L76), [`validateSupport`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.js#L58-L125)).\n     - Traces execution step-by-step using `sys.settrace` and AST inspection (or offline via [`PythonExecutionEngine.trace`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/engine.js#L140-L276)), saving full variable snapshots (`previous`, `current`, `type`, `status: created | updated | unchanged`), loop iterations, condition operands & boolean outcomes, function calls, and return values.\n   - **Rule-Based Teaching System ([explainer.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/explainer.py) & [explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/explainer.js))**:\n     - Generates deterministic **Beginner Mode** and **Technical Mode** explanations, symbol definitions (`PYTHON_SYMBOLS_LIBRARY`), practic\n<truncated 1925 bytes>\nPanel B — Execution Visualizer (Center)**: Algorithm purpose banner, Practice Mode prediction card, step metrics, operation breakdown, condition/return result, execution summary, and visual SVG Control Flow Graph.\n   - **Panel C — Variable Inspector & Built-In Questions (Right)**: Live variable table (`Variable | Previous | Current | Type | State`), visual `nums[i]` array index strip, clickable variable change history, and **9 Built-In Code Questions**.\n   - **Panel D — Step-by-Step Beginner Explanation (Bottom)**: All **7 required explanation cards** (*1. What Current Line Does*, *2. Important Symbols*, *3. Why Line Executes Now*, *4. Variables Before Step*, *5. Changes After Step*, *6. Why Condition is T/F*, *7. Next Line & Why*) with **Beginner Mode** and **Technical Mode** toggle.\n\n4. **Automated Test Suite & Local Server (Sections 14 & 15)**\n   - **[test_engine.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/test_engine.py)**: 12 unit tests covering default `maxSubArray` ($\\rightarrow$ `6`), all-negative `[-5, -2, -8]` ($\\rightarrow$ `-2`), positive numbers ($\\rightarrow$ `10`), single-element, empty list `IndexError`, invalid input, syntax errors, unsupported constructs, infinite loop timeout protection, runtime exceptions, step snapshot restoration, and nested loops.\n   - **[server.py](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/server.py)** & **[README.md](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/README.md)**: Local server and Windows instructions.\n\n---\n\n### How to Run & Test\n1. **Instant Offline Mode**: Open [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/index.html) directly in any browser.\n2. **Run Unit Tests**:\n   ```powershell\n   cd C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\n   python -m unittest test_engine.py -v\n   ```\n3. **Run Local Python Server**:\n   ```powershell\n   cd C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\n   python server.py\n   ```","thinking":"The project requires a thorough review of the generated files to confirm completeness and structural integrity. Examination will focus on verifying proper linking and ensuring there are no residual discrepancies. This check applies to both the HTML and CSS files.\n\n\nThe initial assessment identifies several files needing review, including JavaScript, Python, and CSS components, as well as documentation. The key consideration is the previous behavior where a function call required UI confirmation due to a non-workspace directory; this means subsequent calls won't block execution.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
